From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a maximized Linux program keeps its frame's size when it resizes itself

GTK sizes its own window for a new display scale, which Linux programs now
take while they run (sg-session's XSETTINGS manager): twice as large from
100% to 150%, half again back at 100%. In a maximized frame the window was
then cut off, or left a blank margin in the frame (Thunderbird,
2026-10-05). The frame of a maximized or full-screen program kept its size
but left the program's window at the size it gave itself; it now puts it
back to the frame's, as a window manager holds a maximized window to its
size. A restored program still sizes itself and its frame follows.

Test: test/embedscale-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_EMBED_MAX_FOLLOWS);
test/linuxembed-gate.sh, embeddragmax, embedmaxgrab, csdframe still pass.
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/sg_embed.c
@@ -1017,9 +1017,28 @@
         /* not while maximized or full screen: the frame's size is the
          * screen's then, as a window manager keeps it */
         BOOL fixed;
+        int fx = 0, fy = 0, fw = 0, fh = 0;
         pthread_mutex_lock( &embed_mutex );
         fixed = (e = find_hwnd( hwnd )) && (e->maximized || e->fullscreen);
+        if (fixed) { child = e->child; fx = e->x; fy = e->y; fw = e->w; fh = e->h; }
         pthread_mutex_unlock( &embed_mutex );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_EMBED_MAX_FOLLOWS
+        /* and the program's window is put back to it, as a window manager
+         * holds a maximized window to its size: GTK resizes its own for a
+         * new display scale -- twice as large at 150%, half at 100%, cut
+         * off or a blank margin in its maximized frame */
+        if (fixed && child && (data = get_win_data( hwnd )))
+        {
+            display = data->display;
+            X11DRV_expect_error( display, ignore_error, NULL );
+            pthread_mutex_lock( &embed_mutex );
+            if ((e = find_hwnd( hwnd )) && e->display == display) e->serial = NextRequest( display );
+            pthread_mutex_unlock( &embed_mutex );
+            XMoveResizeWindow( display, child, fx, fy, max( 1, fw ), max( 1, fh ) );
+            X11DRV_check_error();
+            release_win_data( data );
+        }
+#endif
         if (fixed) return 0;
 #endif
         if (!(data = get_win_data( hwnd ))) return 0;
